heads of state and government arrived  for this crucial eu summit to agree  strategy for the next five years sign  association agreements with ukraine  moldova and georgia and decide on their  nomination for the head of europe's  executive branch  the month following the european  elections has seen the usual horse  trading over the eu's future direction  and its top posts what's unusual is it's  ended with an almighty row over the  presidency of the european commission  with 26 member states full square behind  jean-claude juncker and just two britain  and hungary dead against it is not right  for the elected heads of government of  the european countries to give up their  right to  nominate the head of the european  commission the most important role in  europe that is a bad principle and it's  the wrong person eu leaders usually take  the decision by consensus not this time  mr cameron insisted on a vote which he  lost by the expected margin  this is a bad day for europe it risks  undermining the position of national  governments it risks undermining the  power of national parliaments and it  hands new power to the european  parliament among meps whose job it will  be to vote on mr juncker's nomination in  july there was evident relief that the  will of the people as expressed in may's  election was followed through on  if he gets to power will be more  committed to the european parliament and  via this to the european citizens than  all other commission's presidents before  this was not to overshadow other  important items on the agenda not least  the signing finally of an association  agreement with ukraine  i think this is the  most important day for ukrainian history  after  independence day
 

